WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.658
A practical starting pattern is one front end with multiple inference nodes.

00:00:05.658 --> 00:00:13.412
The front end provides a stable user or application interface, while each worker hosts a model server.

00:00:13.412 --> 00:00:20.746
A router or load balancer sends requests only to workers capable of serving the requested model.

00:00:20.746 --> 00:00:31.853
Replicating the same model across several nodes increases concurrent capacity and creates options for maintenance or failure, provided the routing layer removes unhealthy instances promptly.

00:00:31.853 --> 00:00:34.996
Another pattern assigns separate model roles.

00:00:34.996 --> 00:00:46.522
One node may serve a general language model, another a coding model, and a smaller CPU or GPU service may generate embeddings or rerank search results.

00:00:46.522 --> 00:00:53.437
Role separation makes resource use predictable and prevents a large model from evicting smaller services.

00:00:53.437 --> 00:01:01.610
CPU support nodes can host APIs, queues, databases, observability, and retrieval components, preserving expensive GPU capacity for inference.

00:01:01.610 --> 00:01:05.172
Storage and management may also be separated.

00:01:05.172 --> 00:01:12.088
A storage node can hold controlled model versions and distribute them to local worker caches.

00:01:12.088 --> 00:01:17.327
A management node can provide configuration, monitoring, secrets, and deployment coordination.

00:01:17.327 --> 00:01:22.146
Avoid making either service an undocumented single point of failure.

00:01:22.146 --> 00:01:29.481
Define what happens when shared storage, the router, name resolution, or the management plane is unavailable.

00:01:29.481 --> 00:01:33.043
Local clusters favor privacy and predictable ownership.

00:01:33.043 --> 00:01:37.025
Cloud clusters favor rapid provisioning and elastic capacity.

00:01:37.025 --> 00:01:44.360
Hybrid designs can combine them, but data classification and routing policy must make the boundary explicit.

00:01:44.360 --> 00:01:48.760
Start with the fewest roles that meet the requirement.

00:01:48.760 --> 00:02:01.124
Add replication, queues, and management services in response to observed failure or capacity needs, because every architectural box becomes software that must be secured, monitored, upgraded, and recovered.
